SUMMARY:FASEB: Chromatin and Epigenetics in Aging and Disease 2026
LOCATION:The Grand Hotel Malahide\, Malahide\, Ireland
DESCRIPTION:FASEB Science Research Conference on chromatin and epigenetic c
 hange as a driver of ageing and age-related disease. Small residential for
 mat (invited talks plus poster-only submitted abstracts)\, held at a singl
 e hotel venue over four days.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★): mTOR does 
 not appear in the title or in the published programme\, and the connection
  is indirect: epigenetic drift is a separate hallmark of ageing from nutri
 ent sensing\, and the two are linked mainly through metabolite availabilit
 y for chromatin-modifying enzymes (acetyl-CoA\, SAM\, alpha-ketoglutarate)
 . Listed because this is where the ageing-epigenetics community meets and 
 because that metabolite link is the plausible interface with mTORC1-driven
  anabolism\, not because any mTOR content is advertised.\n\nConference sit
 e: https://events.faseb.org/event/Chromatin/summary\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR At
